+# Adopted AE4 support-loss mode-frequency cutoff
+
+Owner tag: `BHSM-AE4-MODE-FREQUENCY-CUTOFF-2026-10-07`.
+Starting revision: `20849fe1f8fae375c011b9eea1b70c400ebe6a1c`.
+Scientific reference: `524ed90689bd5923c249bba2e699abf627e703cd`.
+
+Norman's October 7 continuation explicitly adopts this clarification of the
+existing AE4 cutoff energy. It resolves the previous definition-level energy
+identification; the older reconciliation and its executed outputs remain
+historical evidence. It supplies no numerical event, mode or operator action.
+
+At **AE4's own first-future support-loss event**, continuously transport the
+action-selected physical formation branch to obtain psi_star. With the same
+owned geometric/action pairing, define
+
+\[
+ R_* = \gamma_* J_\Sigma+H_{\rm impedance},\quad
+ r=\langle\psi_*,R_*\psi_*\rangle,\quad
+ i=\langle\psi_*,I_*\psi_*\rangle>0.
+\]
+
+Here I_star is the positive kinetic inertia in the retained physical-clock
+equation `I_lambda D_tau^2 a_lambda+R_lambda a_lambda=f_lambda`. At a valid
+cutoff r is positive. Neither positivity of the Jacobi contribution separately
+nor equality of a symbolic reference length with ell_star is assumed.
+In natural units,
+
+\[
+ E_{\rm impedance}=\sqrt{r/i},\qquad
+ E_{\rm core}=\sqrt{\langle\psi_*,H_{\rm event,drive}\psi_*\rangle/i},\qquad
+ \ell_*=1/E_{\rm impedance},\quad c_*=\ell_*^2=i/r.
+\]
+
+Thus the energy is a **frequency**, not the stiffness eigenvalue itself.
+The action's clock/inertia makes `c_star P_strat` dimensionless. No measured
+particle quantity, fitted scale, new coupling or constitutive function enters.
+The complete surface Jacobi contraction is retained once.
+
+The event requires BOTH energy equality and cessation of outward spacetime
+support. With the same positive inertia and mode, equality is equivalent to
+`<psi_star,(R_star-H_event,drive)psi_star>=0`; it does not require a new
+lowest-eigenvalue selection. Initial RHO-B2 formation, persistence and AE4
+support loss remain distinct unless the action proves coincidence. A C2 cut,
+last cached node or canonical stop is not this event by default.
+
+For x=v and y=J, use **total** branch contractions. They include all applicable
+mode embedding, event, pairing/inertia, normalization, domain and source-map
+motion on a common pullback exactly once:
+
+\[
+ c_x=i_x/r-i r_x/r^2,
+ \quad c_{xy}=i_{xy}/r-(i_xr_y+i_yr_x+i r_{xy})/r^2
+                    +2i r_xr_y/r^3.
+\]
+
+No bare Hellmann-Feynman assumption about R is made. A contraction along the
+moving selected surface already contains event motion and must not receive
+another crossing correction. Real-coordinate Hessian coefficients extend
+linearly to the retained complex current weights, without conjugating them.
+The helper functions evaluate supplied contractions; they do not select the
+physical branch, certify its domain or manufacture unknown terms as zero.
+
+The new targeted controls check total resistance, required Jacobi input,
+frequency/length identities, nondefault length, mixed quotient differentiation,
+complex-linear current extension and once-only surface motion. The control
+inputs are arithmetic examples, not BHSM physical operands or uncertainty
+bounds. Only two affected legacy contract checks are reused; their historical
+materializer and production tests are not run.
